{
  "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/deploymentTemplate.json#",
  "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "description": "Lab (Cisco VLAN Switching - CML) - single VM deployed from a SPECIALIZED Compute Gallery image so the environment comes up already-configured: a Windows Server host VM with Hyper-V, the NAT virtual switch, and the Cisco Modeling Labs (CML) nested VM already installed, network-configured and licensed (parameters('cmlImageId')). Because the image is SPECIALIZED, the VM boots with its existing local accounts, computer name, Hyper-V configuration and nested CML VM intact - there is NO osProfile and NO customData, since either would try to reprovision/rename the machine and could disturb the baked-in Hyper-V/CML state. The candidate RDPs to the VM, opens the CML web UI at https://192.168.100.10 from inside that session, and performs the VLAN configuration task on the IOL L2 switch node.",
    "comments": "ENVIRONMENT BRING-UP: The VM uses a SPECIALIZED image captured from a working, hand-configured environment (Hyper-V nested virtualization enabled, NATSwitch + NAT configured, CML installed/licensed/images imported, VLAN-LAB topology built). NO first-time configuration runs at deploy time. Nested virtualization must be supported by the chosen vmSize (Dsv4/Dv3/Ev3 family or later) or the CML nested VM will fail to start with a 'virtualization disabled' error identical to what was seen during initial setup. PREREQUISITES: the deploying identity needs Reader on the gallery 'Cisco_image' (RG cloudlabs-mgmt-images), or the image shared to the target subscription."
  },
  "parameters": {
    "adminUsername": {
      "type": "string",
      "defaultValue": "azureuser"
    },
    "adminPassword": {
      "type": "securestring",
      "defaultValue": "Mypassword!123"
    },
    "DeploymentID": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "cmlImageId": {
      "type": "string",
      "defaultValue": "/subscriptions/f9d94d2c-5796-4609-94e2-2684e2f14210/resourceGroups/cloudlabs-mgmt-images/providers/Microsoft.Compute/galleries/Cisco_image_migrated/images/Cisco-Switching/versions/1.0.0",
      "metadata": {
        "description": "Resource ID of the SPECIALIZED Compute Gallery image version for the Cisco-Switching lab VM (Hyper-V host + nested CML, pre-configured)."
      }
    }
  },
  "variables": {
    "virtualMachineSize": "Standard_D8as_v7",
    "virtualNetworkName": "[concat('labvNet-', parameters('DeploymentID'))]",
    "mgmtSubnetName": "mgmt",
    "mgmtSubnetPrefix": "10.0.0.0/24",
    "addressPrefix": "10.0.0.0/16",
    "vmName": "[concat('labvm-', parameters('DeploymentID'))]",
    "networkInterfaceName": "[concat('labvm-', parameters('DeploymentID'), '-nic')]",
    "networkSecurityGroupName": "[concat('labvm-', parameters('DeploymentID'), '-nsg')]",
    "publicIpAddressName": "[concat('labvm-', parameters('DeploymentID'), '-pip')]",
    "publicIpAddressDNSName": "[concat('labvm', parameters('DeploymentID'), uniqueString(resourceGroup().id))]",
    "subnetRef": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks/subnets/', variables('virtualNetworkName'), variables('mgmtSubnetName'))]",
    "location": "[resourceGroup().location]"
  },
  "resources": [
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks",
      "apiVersion": "2017-04-01",
      "name": "[variables('virtualNetworkName')]",
      "location": "[variables('location')]",
      "properties": {
        "addressSpace": {
          "addressPrefixes": [ "[variables('addressPrefix')]" ]
        },
        "subnets": [
          {
            "name": "[variables('mgmtSubnetName')]",
            "properties": {
              "addressPrefix": "[variables('mgmtSubnetPrefix')]"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Network/publicIpAddresses",
      "apiVersion": "2017-08-01",
      "name": "[variables('publicIpAddressName')]",
      "location": "[variables('location')]",
      "sku": {
        "name": "Standard"
      },
      "properties": {
        "publicIpAllocationMethod": "Static",
        "dnsSettings": {
          "domainNameLabel": "[variables('publicIpAddressDNSName')]"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Network/networkSecurityGroups",
      "apiVersion": "2017-06-01",
      "name": "[variables('networkSecurityGroupName')]",
      "comments": "Allows RDP (3389) inbound so the student can connect to the Windows host VM and reach the CML web UI (192.168.100.10) from inside that session.",
      "location": "[variables('location')]",
      "properties": {
        "securityRules": [
          {
            "name": "default-allow-rdp",
            "properties": {
              "priority": 110,
              "protocol": "TCP",
              "access": "Allow",
              "direction": "Inbound",
              "sourceAddressPrefix": "*",
              "sourcePortRange": "*",
              "destinationAddressPrefix": "*",
              "destinationPortRange": "3389"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Network/networkInterfaces",
      "apiVersion": "2016-09-01",
      "name": "[variables('networkInterfaceName')]",
      "comments": "Windows host VM NIC - runs Hyper-V + the nested CML VM, reachable over RDP to drive the lab.",
      "location": "[variables('location')]",
      "dependsOn": [
        "[concat('Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks/', variables('virtualNetworkName'))]",
        "[concat('Microsoft.Network/publicIpAddresses/', variables('publicIpAddressName'))]",
        "[concat('Microsoft.Network/networkSecurityGroups/', variables('networkSecurityGroupName'))]"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "ipConfigurations": [
          {
            "name": "ipconfig1",
            "properties": {
              "subnet": {
                "id": "[variables('subnetRef')]"
              },
              "privateIPAllocationMethod": "Dynamic",
              "publicIpAddress": {
                "id": "[resourceId(resourceGroup().name, 'Microsoft.Network/publicIpAddresses', variables('publicIpAddressName'))]"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "networkSecurityGroup": {
          "id": "[resourceId(resourceGroup().name, 'Microsoft.Network/networkSecurityGroups', variables('networkSecurityGroupName'))]"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines",
      "apiVersion": "2019-07-01",
      "name": "[variables('vmName')]",
      "comments": "Windows Server host VM (labvm-<DeploymentID>) built from a SPECIALIZED Compute Gallery image with Hyper-V, the NAT virtual switch, and the nested CML VM (installed, licensed, images imported, VLAN-LAB topology built) pre-baked in. A specialized image carries its own machine identity/local accounts, so this VM has NO osProfile - RDP uses the credentials baked into the image. The candidate RDPs in, opens the CML web UI, and performs the VLAN task on the switch node.",
      "location": "[variables('location')]",
      "dependsOn": [
        "[concat('Microsoft.Network/networkInterfaces/', variables('networkInterfaceName'))]"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "hardwareProfile": {
          "vmSize": "[variables('virtualMachineSize')]"
        },
        "storageProfile": {
          "imageReference": {
            "id": "[parameters('cmlImageId')]"
          },
          "osDisk": {
            "createOption": "fromImage",
            "name": "[concat(variables('vmName'), '-osdisk')]",
            "managedDisk": {
              "storageAccountType": "Standard_LRS"
            }
          },
          "dataDisks": []
        },
        "networkProfile": {
          "networkInterfaces": [
            {
              "id": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/networkInterfaces', variables('networkInterfaceName'))]"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "outputs": {
    "Deployment ID": {
      "type": "string",
      "value": "[parameters('DeploymentID')]"
    },
    "LABVM Admin Username": {
      "type": "string",
      "value": "[parameters('adminUsername')]"
    },
    "LABVM Admin Password": {
      "type": "string",
      "value": "[parameters('adminPassword')]"
    },
    "LABVM DNS Name": {
      "type": "string",
      "value": "[reference(resourceId('Microsoft.Network/publicIPAddresses', variables('publicIpAddressName'))).dnsSettings.fqdn]"
    },
    "LABVM RDP Command": {
      "type": "string",
      "value": "[concat('mstsc /v:', reference(resourceId('Microsoft.Network/publicIPAddresses', variables('publicIpAddressName'))).dnsSettings.fqdn)]"
    }
  }
}
